      <ArticleTitle>Ustekinumab targeting IL-23 in moderate-to-severe Crohn's disease: a randomized trial.</ArticleTitle>
      <Abstract>
        <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND">Interleukin-23 (IL-23) is a key driver of mucosal inflammation in Crohn's disease.</AbstractText>
        <AbstractText Label="METHODS">We randomized 300 patients to ustekinumab or placebo and measured clinical remission at week 44.</AbstractText>
        <AbstractText Label="RESULTS">Clinical remission was achieved in 53% of ustekinumab-treated patients versus 36% of placebo (p&lt;0.01).</AbstractText>
        <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS">IL-23 blockade with ustekinumab is effective for maintenance of remission in Crohn's disease.</AbstractText>
      </Abstract>
